      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is deeply unsettling to feel like a glitch, a placeholder where a real self used to be. You're right; the expectation to \"just keep going\" when your internal world has fundamentally shifted is a cruel, unacknowledged demand. If the social self is gone, the next step is to explore what little remains—even if it's just the quiet, empty space you're currently occupying. A therapist can help you start mapping out what that \"glitch\" might be capable of, even if it's just surviving the next hour.",
